settings.custom_liquid:
{%- comment -%}
  Joy — "Build your subscription" CTA (SB-16593)

  HOW TO INSTALL: Theme editor -> Product template -> "Product information" section
  -> Add block -> "Custom Liquid" -> paste this ENTIRE file into the box -> drag the
  block to sit directly under "Buy buttons".

  No theme code to edit. No app extension needed.

  Only Fixed Bundle products get it: on any other product this renders nothing, so it
  is safe to leave on the shared Product template.

  What it does: leaves the theme's own Add to cart alone and adds a card inviting the
  shopper to build a subscription instead. The app's subscription widget is hidden,
  because these boxes are not discounted and "Subscribe & Save" would promise a saving
  that does not exist. Subscriptions are built on the builder page, which the main
  navigation also links to.

  TO CHANGE THE BUILDER PAGE: edit the BUILDER_URL line below. A URL that already has a
  query string is fine - the `?` / `&` separator is picked automatically.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign BUILDER_URL = '/pages/build-your-subscription' -%}

{%- if product.metafields.avada_fixed_bundle.data and BUILDER_URL != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The builder page may already carry a query string: this shop reaches it as
    `/pages/build-your-subscription`, because the landing is
    an alternate view rather than a page of its own. Hard-coding `?bundle=` there produces
    a second `?`, which Shopify reads as part of the `view` value - the page falls back to
    the default template and the builder never renders.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if BUILDER_URL contains '?' -%}
    {%- assign jbc_sep = '&' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign jbc_sep = '?' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign jbc_target = BUILDER_URL | append: jbc_sep | append: 'bundle=' | append: product.handle -%}

  <div class="jbc-card">
    <span class="jbc-icon" aria-hidden="true">🌿</span>
    <div class="jbc-body">
      <p class="jbc-title">Want this regularly?</p>
      <p class="jbc-text">
        Build a flexible subscription with your favourite essentials. Choose a seasonal box,
        add your staples, then top up with one off items whenever you like.
      </p>
      <a class="jbc-link" href="{{ jbc_target }}">Build a subscription →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    /* Only the app widget is hidden. The theme's Add to cart, quantity stepper and
       sticky bar all stay: this product is bought outright like any other, and the
       subscription path is the card above. */
    .Avada-SubscriptionWidget-Block {
      display: none !important;
    }

    .jbc-card {
{%- comment -%}
        The theme's --font-body-family holds an unquoted "DM Sans 9pt"; the `9pt` token
        invalidates any font-family that reads it, so this card would render in Times.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if settings.custom_font2 != blank %}
      font-family: "{{ settings.custom_font2 }}", sans-serif;
      {%- endif %}
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 14px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 18px 20px;
      margin: 16px 0;
      background: #f6f7f5;
    }
    .jbc-icon {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      width: 40px;
      height: 40px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: #fff;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1;
    }
    .jbc-body { min-width: 0; }
    .jbc-title {
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 16px;
      margin: 0 0 6px;
      color: #1a1a1a;
    }
    .jbc-text {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #4a4a4a;
    }
    /* Brand green set explicitly: without it the theme's default anchor colour wins and
       the link renders browser-blue. */
    .jbc-link,
    .jbc-link:visited,
    .jbc-link:hover {
      display: inline-block;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 15px;
      color: rgb(8, 108, 63);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .jbc-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
